(e) Attending a surveyor, when ordered by a court, per deputy or sheriff assigned ........................................................ 20.00;
(f) Taking any bond that he is authorized or required to take in any action ..................................................................... 5.00;
(g) Collecting money under execution or distress warrant, if the debt is paid or the property sold, or a delivery bond given and not complied with, six percent (6%) on the first three hundred dollars ($300) and three percent (3%) on the residue; when he or she levies an execution or distress warrant, and the defendant replevies the debt, or the writ is stayed by legal proceedings or by the order of the plaintiff, half of the above commissions, to be charged to the plaintiff and collected as costs in the case;
(h) Taking a recognizance of a witness ........................................................... 3.00;
